    <statement><p>Evaluate the iterated integral:</p>
<p><me>\int_{0}^{7} \int_{3}^{8} \sqrt{x+4 y} \,dx \,dy</me>
Answer : <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>150.663</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>y</m> as a constant. Then we evaluate the resulting integral with respect to <m>y</m>:



<me>\begin{array}{l}
\int_{0}^{7}\int_{3}^{8}\sqrt{x+4 y} \,dx \,dy \\
=\int_{0}^{7} \frac{2}{3}{( x+4 y )}^{3/2}\bigg|_{x=3}^{8} \,dy \\
=\int_{0}^{7}\frac{2}{3}\left({( {8}+4 y )}^{3/2}-{( {3}+4 y )}^{3/2}\right)dy  \\
=\frac{2}{3}\left(\frac{2}{5\cdot 4}{( 8+4 y)}^{5/2}
-\frac{2}{5\cdot 4}{( 3+4 y )}^{5/2}\right) \bigg|_{0}^{7} \\
=\frac{1}{15}\left(\left({36}^{5/2}-{31}^{5/2}\right)-\left({8}^{5/2}-{3}^{5/2}\right)\right) \\
=\frac{1}{15}\left({36}^{5/2}-{31}^{5/2}-{8}^{5/2}+{3}^{5/2}\right)\approx 150.663
\end{array}</me>



</solution>
